 look (underlined, Iris, sans face); the app's are neutral underlined mono links that open in a new tab.","Coverage and the Requirements tab of Overview are not here; this is the section of one View.","Every visible string is bound with $i18n except identities and the provider's Rule text; en-US and zh-TW keep identical key sets.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["A member scrolled the Spec tab of the right panel of a View to §8; the panel is 340px wide at the right edge and scrolls (§1 to §7 are Views of their own).","The base state is the View Checkout in a Workspace whose requirement source is a `spec` provider that was read: five references: two that the View's Spec lists, one that only two Variants list, one that only a Variant lists, and one ID the source does not have.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset, one Locale and one theme; below 640px a phone reads the section folded behind its title."],"intent":"Show the requirement references of a View's Spec tab as built from Adapter Widgets only: the Requirements section (§8) that lists the requirement IDs the View's Spec and its Variants reference, with what the Workspace's requirement source says of each ID, and how the section reads without a source, with a source that gives links, or when a source cannot be read.","interactionRules":["The section lists the references of the View's Spec first, then the ones only a Variant lists, each ID in mono; the Workbench shows references and never edits them, an Agent adds them through MCP.","With a `spec` provider that was read, each ID shows the Rule text the source has for it; an ID the source does not have says \"Not in the source\" and is kept as written.","A reference that only a Variant lists names the Variant behind it, one badge per Variant.","With no provider, or a source that cannot be read, nothing checks the IDs: every ID says \"Unverified\" and no Rule text is show